==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*per- (fare)}}
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:practice<alt:practice, practique, practyse><ety:der<practicen<alt:practicen, practisen, practizen, practysen><ety:der<frm:pratiser<alt:practiser, pratiser>>>>>|tree=++}}
The noun is from {{inh|en|enm|practice,practique,practyse}}, from the verb; also compare {{cog|la-med|prāctica}}.<ref name="MEDn">{{R:MED Online|entry=practī̆se|pos=n|id=MED34280}}</ref>. Displaced native {{noncog|ang|sidu}}.

The verb is from {{inh|en|enm|practicen,practisen,practizen,practysen}}, from {{der|en|frm|practiser,pratiser}}, an alteration of {{m|frm|practiquer}}, from {{der|en|la-med|prācticō}}, from {{der|en|la-lat|prācticus}}, from {{der|en|grc|πρακτικός}}.<ref>{{R:Collins English Dictionary}}</ref><ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary|pos=v}}</ref>

The spelling {{m|en||practice}} is attested once in Middle English for both the noun and the verb.<ref name="MEDn"/><ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=practī̆sen|pos=v|id=MED34282}}</ref> The noun began to be assimilated in spelling to nouns in {{m|en||-ice}};<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary|pos=n}}</ref> {{m|en|practise#Noun|pos=noun}} is now obsolete.

